tree":[6.6,162.7,12.3,5.2]},{"tree":[27.4,150.1,13.0,5.5]},{"tree":[45.0,160.9,13.0,5.4]},{"tree":[78.4,152.5,11.3,4.8]},{"tree":[110.9,158.0,9.4,4.0]},{"tree":[127.9,155.7,9.3,3.9]},{"tree":[149.7,154.6,9.4,4.0]},{"tree":[185.8,159.0,12.6,5.3]}],"notes":"Built from sources, no photograph of the built house read (snohetta.com and the architecture press are refused to the session); scripts/model_shanghai_opera.py writes it, and its docstring lists them. Plan: OpenStreetMap way 1316877742 (ODbL), which Overture's ground agrees with; Sentinel-2 of 8 and 14 October 2026 shows the white roof filling it and paved fingers running west from it toward the Huangpu. Heights: 45 m at most (World Construction Network), the roof's public platform 28 m (SmartShanghai) to about 40 m (Xinhua), here 30.6; a double-helix stair in a round well (22-32 m radius, about 295 degrees) climbs to it, here one helix (the two do not part at 3.4 m a voxel); three halls of 2,000, 1,200 and 1,000 seats, so three stage towers, 37-44 m; full-height glass under the white roof (UHPC). Placed after Snøhetta's film of the design (2019) seen from above: the well about 35 m south of the outline's middle, the towers in the south and east, the roof's ribs fanning north and west. Guessed: the way the roof winds (clockwise up from the plaza in the west to its top in the south-south-west), every height between, which tower is which hall, where the glass stands (under every leaf 20.4 m or more up, 13.6 m tall, 6.8 m back), the lower hall in the gap between the roof's top and foot and its glazed face (the 1,000-seat hall's glass wall is about 13 m high; where it stands is not known), the red public hall behind the glass (13,000 m2, not drawn), the park's trees. Refine from photographs and drawings when they can be read."}
